; example.lab. authoritative zone for the Protocol Lab DNS hierarchy (Lab 06).
; Served by the auth node.
; Two names with different TTLs let you contrast short- and long-lived cache
; entries. The SOA minimum (last number) is the negative-cache TTL used for
; NXDOMAIN answers (RFC 2308).
$TTL 3600
example.lab.        IN  SOA ns.example.lab. admin.example.lab. (
                        1          ; serial
                        3600       ; refresh
                        900        ; retry
                        604800     ; expire
                        300 )      ; negative cache TTL (NXDOMAIN)
example.lab.        IN  NS  ns.example.lab.
ns.example.lab.     IN  A   10.0.3.2

; 203.0.113.0/24 is RFC 5737 documentation space. Lab use only.
; Short TTL: watch it count down and re-resolve.
www.example.lab.        60    IN  A   203.0.113.10
; Long TTL: stays cached far longer than www.
stable.example.lab.     3600  IN  A   203.0.113.20
example.lab.            60    IN  A   203.0.113.10
; Note: there is deliberately NO record for missing.example.lab.
; Querying it yields NXDOMAIN plus the SOA above for negative caching.
